WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:03.720
Once you know what's required for success,

00:03.720 --> 00:07.560
it's time for an honest self-assessment.

00:07.560 --> 00:09.880
This is how you identify the gap

00:09.880 --> 00:13.200
between where you are and where you want to be.

00:14.080 --> 00:16.600
These gaps are not weaknesses.

00:16.600 --> 00:18.900
They are opportunities.

00:18.900 --> 00:21.720
They are specific areas you will target

00:21.720 --> 00:24.440
in your 90-day plan.

00:24.440 --> 00:28.120
Looking back at Lynn, her self-assessment was clear.

00:28.120 --> 00:30.340
Mindset, check.

00:30.340 --> 00:32.640
Motivation, check.

00:32.640 --> 00:35.160
Legal experience, check.

00:35.160 --> 00:38.940
Her gaps were in managing people, managing budgets,

00:38.940 --> 00:41.200
and up-to-date industry knowledge.

00:41.200 --> 00:43.840
So, her Make It Happen checklist

00:43.840 --> 00:47.020
focused on closing those specific gaps.

00:47.020 --> 00:49.680
These became her goals.

00:49.680 --> 00:53.080
But a goal like getting better at managing budgets

00:53.080 --> 00:54.560
is not a goal.

00:54.560 --> 00:55.880
It's a wish.

00:55.880 --> 00:59.520
To make it real, we use the SMART framework.

00:59.520 --> 01:00.880
Now, I know many of you say,

01:00.880 --> 01:03.240
I've heard of the SMART goals before.

01:03.240 --> 01:06.560
But remember, this isn't about what you know

01:06.560 --> 01:07.880
or what you've heard.

01:07.880 --> 01:11.320
It's about what you do daily.

01:11.320 --> 01:15.500
An Athleader applies these principles with discipline.

01:15.500 --> 01:20.500
Your goal must be specific, measurable, attainable,

01:20.500 --> 01:22.660
relevant, and time-bound.

01:22.660 --> 01:25.100
Let's look at another example.

01:25.100 --> 01:29.300
Evan is a CFO and a father of a son with autism.

01:29.300 --> 01:32.580
His passion is to launch an online community

01:32.580 --> 01:36.540
to support other parents of children with special needs.

01:36.540 --> 01:38.940
One of the items on his gap checklist

01:38.940 --> 01:42.100
was identifying a technical partner.

01:42.100 --> 01:45.880
A SMART goal that became, within 60 days,

01:45.880 --> 01:50.880
obtain partnership proposals from three qualified vendors

01:50.900 --> 01:54.940
with each proposal detailing the creation

01:54.940 --> 01:58.940
of a scalable online community that includes reporting,

01:58.940 --> 02:03.180
functionality, and content self-management.

02:03.180 --> 02:04.760
Do you see the difference?

02:04.760 --> 02:07.640
It's specific, it's measurable, it's attainable,

02:07.640 --> 02:12.520
it's relevant to his vision, and it's time-bound.

02:12.520 --> 02:15.480
That is a goal you can execute against.

02:15.480 --> 02:17.840
In your playbook, you will assess yourself

02:17.840 --> 02:21.360
against the prerequisites you've identified.

02:21.400 --> 02:25.560
Find your most critical gaps and then transform those gaps

02:25.560 --> 02:29.600
into two or three powerful SMART goals

02:29.600 --> 02:32.380
for your first 90-day season.

